A_592 - When you buy bread it is usual to store it in a paper bag, often inside some cabinet. If you place the paper bag in an airtight sealable plastic bag (like those sometimes used to store certain products in the freezer), then the bread should not dry out because the moisture does not escape and it should stay soft for longer . In addition to this, if the plastic bag were transparent and the bread was left in a non-dark place, perhaps at that point the preservation would be further improved. If a quartz crystal were left nearby, that should also have positive effects. In addition to this, bars, bakers and pastry chefs can also use it at the end of the working day, to better preserve their products while waiting for the next working day. If necessary, you can also just use a simple plastic bag tightly closed with a knot.